From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 02:43:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Lophinya: exp - NyaCore candidate C step 4: route
 WalkNodeEvaluator search through overridable mob accessors

Per DEC-70 3rd section step 4. Every this.mob.X() call inside the search-time
methods (getStart, getNeighbors, findAcceptedNode, getPathTypeOfMob, etc.) now
goes through a small set of protected accessor methods that default to plain
delegation to this.mob - the synchronous path is behaviourally unchanged.
This is the extension point a NavigationSnapshot-based subclass will override
to run the same search algorithm on a worker thread without ever touching a
live Mob/ServerLevel/Chunk object, per the full live-state enumeration in
evidence/20260806-nyacore-candidate-c-navigationsnapshot-design.md.

prepare()/done() are untouched (stay owner-thread-only lifecycle hooks).
getPathTypeOfMob's Mob parameter is now unused in favour of the accessor -
every real caller (this class, FlyNodeEvaluator, SwimNodeEvaluator) already
always passes this.mob, so this changes no behaviour.

